UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Treasury Regulation Section 301.7701-3, the check-the-box rules allow eligible entities to elect their tax classification by filing Form 8832 (Entity Classification Election). A multi-member LLC defaults to partnership treatment but may elect C corporation status via this form.
Wrong (A): Form 1065 is the annual partnership information return, not an entity classification election form.
Wrong (B): Form 2553 is used to elect S corporation status and requires a prior or simultaneous election to be classified as a corporation. It does not change the default entity classification.
Wrong (D): Form 1120 is the annual C corporation income tax return, not the form used to elect corporate tax classification.$EXPL$
